FigJam is mainly a collaborative whiteboarding and brainstorming tool, not a full UI design tool.

It is primarily used for:
=========================
Mind maps
Brainstorming
Sticky notes
User flows
Wireframe planning
Team collaboration
UX workshops
Diagrams
Planning sessions

FigJam vs Figma
================
Feature	                    FigJam	                Figma
=======                     ======                  ======
Mind Mapping	              Excellent	              Basic
Brainstorming	              Excellent	              Limited
Sticky Notes	              Yes	                    No
Whiteboard	                Yes	                    No
UI Design	                  Basic	                  Professional
Prototyping	                Minimal	                Advanced
Components	                Limited	                Full support
Developer Handoff	          Limited	                Full
UX Workshops	              Excellent	              Moderate

Simple Explanation
==================
FigJam
======
Think of it as:
===============
a digital whiteboard
brainstorming canvas
collaborative planning board

Used BEFORE actual UI design.

Figma
=====
Think of it as:

professional UI/UX design software
interface creation tool
prototyping tool

Used FOR actual UI design and development handoff.

Typical Workflow
================
Ideas → FigJam → Figma → Prototype → Development

Example:
========
Brainstorm app features in FigJam
=================================
Create mind maps and user flows
Plan screens and navigation
Move to Figma
Design actual UI screens


Best Use Cases for FigJam
=========================

Use FigJam for:
===============
Mind maps
UX planning
Brainstorming
Affinity mapping
User journey maps
Team meetings
Flowcharts
Research organization

Use Figma for:
==============
Final UI screens
Responsive layouts
Design systems
Components
Interactive prototypes
Developer-ready designs


Start using FigJam, follow these beginner steps:
================================================
1. Open FigJam
==============
You can start FigJam in two ways:
Go to FigJam Official Website
Or type figjam.new directly in your browser.

2. Sign in or Create a Figma Account
====================================
FigJam is part of Figma.
Create a free account using:
Email
Google account

3. Create a New FigJam Board
============================
After logging in:
Click New FigJam Board
A blank infinite whiteboard opens.

4. Learn the Basic Tools
========================
Here are the most-used beginner tools:
Tool                  	      Use
Sticky Notes (S)	            Brainstorm ideas
Text (T)	                    Add headings and notes
Shapes	                      Flowcharts and diagrams
Connector Lines (L)	          Connect ideas
Marker (M)	                  Draw freely
Stamps & Emojis	              Team feedback

5. Start With Simple Activities
===============================
Good beginner exercises:
Brainstorming
Mind maps
Moodboards
User flows
Wireframe planning
Team meeting notes

FigJam is mainly for planning and collaboration, while regular Figma Design files are 
for detailed UI design.

6. Use Templates
================
Click Templates inside FigJam to quickly start with:
Mind maps
Kanban boards
UX research boards
User journey maps
Sprint planning

7. Invite Others
================
Click Share → copy the link → collaborate in real time.

Beginner Workflow in UX/UI
==========================
A common beginner flow is:
Brainstorming
Mind Mapping
Moodboard
User Flow
Wireframe Planning

Move to Figma Design for UI screens


